WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.860 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Adobe agreed to buy Figma for
about twenty billion dollars.

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:05.960 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The acquisition never closed.

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:09.080 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Adobe still paid Figma
one billion dollars.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:12.120 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
That billion dollars was
not a government fine.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.040 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
It was not a court judgment.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.480 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
And it was not part of the
twenty-billion-dollar purchase price.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:21.420 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
It was a contractual termination
payment money Adobe had agreed

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:25.560 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
could become due if the deal
failed under specified closing and

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.300 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
regulatory circumstances.

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:31.000 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The billion-dollar consequence
was not invented after the

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.520 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
acquisition collapsed.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:35.660 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
It had been negotiated before
the merger agreement was even

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:36.700 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
signed.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:40.680 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
So the real story is not simply
why regulators had concerns

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:43.320 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
about Adobe buying Figma.

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:46.520 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
It is how two companies priced
the risk that the deal might

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:50.200 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
never close and how that
risk eventually became a real

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.920 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
one-billion-dollar cash payment.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:56.940 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Figma had become a major
collaborative design platform used by

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:58.180 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
product teams.

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:01.500 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Its value was not just
in drawing interfaces.

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:04.800 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Teams could work in the
same files, comment,

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:07.700 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
prototype, maintain shared design systems

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.380 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
and move work between
design and development.

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:13.460 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Adobe was one of the world's
largest creative-software

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:16.560 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
companies, with products
including Photoshop,

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.120 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Illustrator and Adobe XD.

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:22.480 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
That meant the proposed
acquisition was not just a large

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:24.200 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
financial transaction.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:27.240 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
It connected two companies
whose products touched important

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:31.240 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
parts of the digital-design
workflow, even though Adobe and

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:35.140 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Figma later disputed how
directly their products competed.

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:39.440 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
On September fifteenth, twenty
twenty-two, Adobe and Figma

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:42.020 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
announced a definitive merger agreement.

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:45.860 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The headline number was
approximately twenty billion dollars.

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:49.900 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The consideration was expected
to be roughly half cash and half

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:51.220 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Adobe stock.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:54.460 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
But the agreement did not guarantee
that the transaction would

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:55.360 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
close.

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:58.960 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
It still depended on regulatory
approvals and other closing

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:00.080 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
conditions.

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:02.920 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
And by the time the public
heard the twenty-billion-dollar

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:06.880 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
headline, the contract already
contained another number that

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:09.040 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
would later become just as important.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:11.020 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
One billion dollars.

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:14.480 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The negotiation record filed
with the Securities and Exchange

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:18.060 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Commission shows how that
number entered the deal.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:21.460 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Adobe and Figma had discussed
possible combinations before

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:25.480 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
twenty twenty-two, but those
earlier conversations did not

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:27.180 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
produce a transaction.

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:31.400 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Serious acquisition talks restarted
in April twenty twenty-two.

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:36.160 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
In May, the companies entered
a confidentiality agreement and

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:39.740 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Figma began providing
confidential information to Adobe.

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:41.760 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Then came the price.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:45.740 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
On June nineteenth, twenty
twenty-two, Adobe delivered a

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:49.340 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
non-binding proposal to acquire
Figma for twenty billion

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:53.120 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
dollars, roughly half
cash and half stock.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:56.800 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
That proposal did not yet
include a termination fee.

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:00.180 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Figma did not negotiate
only the headline price.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:03.460 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
It also negotiated what would
happen if the transaction could

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:04.580 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
not close.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:09.580 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
On July fifth, Figma proposed a
reverse termination fee tied to

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:12.880 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
failure to obtain required
antitrust approvals.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.080 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Then, on July twentieth,

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:17.860 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Adobe came back with a revised proposal.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.940 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The twenty-billion-dollar price remained.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:24.500 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
And now the proposal included
a one-billion-dollar reverse

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:26.240 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
termination fee.

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:28.120 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
That sequence matters.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:32.340 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
June nineteenth: twenty
billion dollars, no fee.

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:36.140 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
July fifth: Figma asks for
protection against regulatory

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:37.380 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
failure.

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:38.980 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
July twentieth:

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:43.520 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Adobe agrees to a one-billion-dollar
reverse termination fee.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:46.460 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
More than a year before
the acquisition ended, the

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:50.120 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
billion-dollar cost was already
inside the deal architecture.

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:53.940 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
A reverse termination fee is
not a punishment imposed by the

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:57.660 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
government. It is a risk-allocation
term negotiated by the

00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:58.600 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
parties to a transaction.

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:02.980 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
In simple terms, the buyer
agrees that if specified closing

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:06.920 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
failures occur, the seller
can receive a defined payment.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:10.080 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
In the Adobe-Figma agreement,
the number was one billion

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:14.300 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
dollars. Section eight-point-two
of the merger agreement set out

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:18.120 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
the fee in defined antitrust
and closing circumstances.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:21.740 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
And the contract makes an unusually
useful distinction for this

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:25.220 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
story. It says the termination
fee is not a penalty.

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:29.020 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
It describes the payment
as liquidated damages.

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:32.280 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
So the agreement did more than
describe the deal the companies

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:33.700 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
wanted to close.

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:37.480 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
It also described a financial
consequence if that deal failed

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:39.420 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
under the specified conditions.

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:42.860 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The twenty-billion-dollar
number described the upside.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:46.320 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The one-billion-dollar clause
priced part of the downside.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:49.820 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
On September fifteenth, twenty
twenty-two, the definitive

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:53.460 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
agreement was signed and the
transaction became public.

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:56.980 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Adobe was proposing one of the
largest software acquisitions of

00:04:56.980 --> 00:05:00.940 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
its era. Figma would remain a
separate company until closing,

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:03.680 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
but the plan was for it
to become part of Adobe.

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:06.900 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
At that moment, the story
looked like a conventional giant

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:08.620 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
technology acquisition.

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:09.800 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
A buyer.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:13.320 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
A target. A
twenty-billion-dollar headline.

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:15.660 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Regulatory approvals to obtain.

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:18.740 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
But there was already a
one-billion-dollar failure mechanism

00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:20.180 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
sitting inside the contract.

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:23.300 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
That is easy to miss in
a merger announcement.

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:25.940 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The public headline
is the purchase price.

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:28.920 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The failure terms live deeper
in the agreement, because they

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:31.380 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
matter only if something goes wrong.

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:34.060 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The question was whether
this one ever would.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:37.760 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
In twenty twenty-three, that
question stopped being theoretical.

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:40.680 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The United Kingdom was one
of the first places where the

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:42.340 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
pressure became formal.

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:45.960 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
On May third, twenty twenty-three,
the Competition and Markets

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:49.300 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Authority opened its inquiry
into the proposed acquisition.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:53.220 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
By June thirtieth, the CMA said
there were grounds for deeper

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:54.940 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
competition concerns.

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:58.680 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
On July thirteenth, the transaction
was referred for an in-depth

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:00.380 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Phase Two investigation.

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:03.860 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The European Commission received
formal notification on June

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:07.520 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
thirtieth. On August seventh,
it opened its own in-depth

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:08.740 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
investigation.

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:12.160 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
And in the United States, the
Justice Department's Antitrust

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:15.040 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Division was also
investigating the transaction.

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:18.420 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
These were separate processes
with different procedures.

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:23.180 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The UK and EU reviews developed
formal competition objections.

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:27.080 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The public DOJ record for
this story establishes an

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:30.340 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
investigation, not a
filed merger lawsuit.

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:33.660 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The important business point was
that signing and closing were

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:35.140 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
two different events.

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:38.540 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Adobe and Figma already had
a merger agreement, but the

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:41.200 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
companies still needed the
required approvals before the

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:43.160 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
transaction could actually be completed.

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:47.300 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
As the reviews deepened, the
one-billion-dollar clause did not

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:48.340 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
change.

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:51.260 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
What changed was the chance that
the companies might eventually

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:54.400 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
need it. The fee mattered because
it had already been written

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:58.000 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
into their own contract, and the
possibility of a failed closing

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:00.220 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
was becoming harder to ignore.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:05.140 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
By November twenty twenty-three,
the UK and EU concerns had

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:06.980 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
become much more explicit.

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:10.900 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
On November seventeenth, the
European Commission adopted a

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:12.720 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Statement of Objections.

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:16.860 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
That was a formal statement of
preliminary concerns, not a final

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:18.520 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
prohibition decision.

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:22.820 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Then, on November twenty-eighth,
the UK CMA published

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:24.520 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
provisional findings.

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:28.800 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The CMA provisionally identified
competition concerns involving

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:33.060 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
all-in-one product design,
vector editing and raster editing

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:36.980 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
software. The same day, it
published a notice of possible

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:37.920 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
remedies.

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:42.080 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Those possible remedies included
prohibition of the merger and

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:43.960 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
structural divestitures.

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:47.400 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
That was a major escalation
in practical terms.

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:50.100 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
A provisional concern is one thing.

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:53.140 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
A remedies discussion forces
the parties to confront what the

00:07:53.140 --> 00:07:56.860 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
deal might have to look like if
the concerns are not resolved.

00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:01.640 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The CMA document also discussed
a possible divestiture of Figma

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:05.300 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Design and said that remedy
would be substantially similar to

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:08.720 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
prohibition while
introducing additional risks.

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:10.800 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The pressure was real.

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:14.920 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
But neither the CMA nor the
European Commission had issued a

00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:17.420 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
final decision prohibiting
the transaction.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:21.740 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The final legal "no" had not yet arrived.

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:25.300 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Adobe and Figma did not accept
the regulators' theories as

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:26.580 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
settled fact.

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:30.260 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
In their submissions to the CMA,
the companies argued that their

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:32.900 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
products and capabilities
were complementary.

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:36.820 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
They argued that the transaction
would be pro-competitive.

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:40.100 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
And they strongly disagreed
with the provisional findings.

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:44.040 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
That counter-position belongs
in the film for a simple reason:

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:48.500 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
neither the UK nor the EU
process reached a final merits

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:49.540 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
decision.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:53.680 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The public record contains serious
regulatory concerns, but it

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:56.820 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
also contains the companies'
detailed disagreement with those

00:08:56.820 --> 00:08:57.740 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
concerns.

00:08:58.340 --> 00:09:01.580 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
By December, the argument had
shifted toward what kinds of

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:05.020 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
remedies could realistically
address the regulators' concerns.

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:08.860 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
On December fourteenth, Adobe and
Figma submitted their response

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:11.200 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
to the CMA's remedies notice.

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:14.780 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
In that response, the companies
argued that the direction of the

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:18.220 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
possible remedies effectively
pointed toward either prohibition

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:21.360 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
or divestiture of Figma Design.

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:23.800 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
That was the companies' characterization.

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:26.700 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
It was not a final CMA ruling.

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:30.260 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
But it captures how narrow
they said the path had become.

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:34.820 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
No final UK or EU prohibition
order had been issued.

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:37.900 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Yet the practical question
was now unavoidable.

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:41.620 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Could this transaction still
reach the approvals required to

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:42.460 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
close?

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:46.060 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The final move came from
Adobe and Figma themselves.

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:49.780 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
On December seventeenth, twenty
twenty-three, the companies

00:09:49.780 --> 00:09:53.220 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
approved and signed a mutual
termination agreement.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:57.060 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The next day, they announced
that the acquisition was over.

00:09:57.120 --> 00:09:59.520 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Their public explanation was direct.

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:02.580 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
They said there was no clear
path to obtaining the necessary

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:06.420 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
regulatory approvals from the
European Commission and the UK

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:07.900 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
CMA.

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:11.240 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
That is different from saying a
regulator had already issued a

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:13.020 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
final prohibition order.

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:17.260 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The companies ended the deal by
mutual agreement before final UK

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:20.360 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
and EU merits decisions arrived.

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:25.060 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
After the abandonment, the CMA
cancelled its Phase Two inquiry.

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:28.600 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The European Commission's
investigation ended without a formal

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:30.860 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Commission decision on the merits.

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:34.440 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
And in the United States, the
Justice Department's Antitrust

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:38.480 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Division publicly welcomed the
abandonment and confirmed that it

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:40.300 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
had investigated the transaction.

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:44.560 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The public Stage One record does
not show a DOJ merger lawsuit

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:47.660 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
or a court judgment blocking the deal.

00:10:47.900 --> 00:10:51.740 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
So the transaction did not end
with a final courtroom loss.

00:10:51.820 --> 00:10:55.240 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
It ended with a mutual termination
after the companies said they

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:58.840 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
no longer saw a clear path
to the approvals they needed.

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:02.000 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
And that is the moment the
billion-dollar clause stopped being

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:03.000 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
theoretical.

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:06.540 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The mutual termination
agreement did not just end the

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:06.900 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
acquisition.

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:09.960 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
It specified what happened next.

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:13.840 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Adobe was required to pay Figma
one billion dollars in cash

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:16.140 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
within three business days.

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:20.120 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The agreement described that
payment as liquidated damages.

00:11:20.580 --> 00:11:24.320 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
It also made the payment Figma's
sole and exclusive remedy under

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:25.820 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
the merger agreement.

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:29.860 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
On December twentieth, twenty
twenty-three, Adobe paid.

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:33.520 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Adobe later disclosed
that it used cash on hand.

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:36.100 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Figma later disclosed
that it received the same

00:11:36.100 --> 00:11:38.420 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
one-billion-dollar payment.

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:41.440 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Those later filings are important
because they confirm the

00:11:41.440 --> 00:11:44.100 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
consequence from both
sides of the transaction.

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:48.300 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The fee was not merely a number
left in an abandoned contract.

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:51.000 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
It became an actual transfer of cash.

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:54.840 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
On December seventeenth, the
companies ended the merger.

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:59.000 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Three days later, the
one-billion-dollar clause became cash.

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:00.240 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The acquisition disappeared.

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:02.980 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The termination fee did not.

00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:06.020 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
And the payment did not come
from a regulator's invoice.

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:09.680 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
It came from a contract the
companies had negotiated themselves.

00:12:10.280 --> 00:12:13.580 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
This story has two giant
numbers, and they mean completely

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:15.020 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
different things.

00:12:15.180 --> 00:12:17.640 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
About twenty billion dollars
was the proposed acquisition

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:19.060 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
consideration.

00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:22.340 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
That was the amount associated
with the deal Adobe wanted to

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:23.240 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
close.

00:12:23.460 --> 00:12:27.220 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Because the acquisition never
closed, Adobe did not pay Figma

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:29.860 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
twenty billion dollars
to buy the company.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:33.540 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
One billion dollars was the
actual termination payment.

00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:35.080 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Adobe paid it.

00:12:35.080 --> 00:12:36.760 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Figma received it.

00:12:36.760 --> 00:12:40.040 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Adobe later recorded the
one-billion-dollar fee in operating

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:41.240 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
expenses.

00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:44.160 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Figma recorded the
payment in other income.

00:12:44.420 --> 00:12:46.140 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Those are separate categories.

00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:49.100 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The accounting records make
the distinction concrete.

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:51.680 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Adobe treated the fee as an expense.

00:12:51.980 --> 00:12:54.340 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Figma treated the receipt as income.

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:57.160 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Neither filing turns the
abandoned twenty-billion-dollar

00:12:57.160 --> 00:13:00.640 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
purchase price into
money that changed hands.

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:04.380 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Adobe did not spend twenty-one
billion dollars on Figma.

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:07.260 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
One number described a
purchase that never happened.

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:10.040 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The other described the contractual
payment that survived the

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:11.160 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
failed deal.

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:15.260 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
That is the billion-dollar cost
at the center of this story.

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:18.500 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The failed acquisition
did not end Figma's story.

00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:20.600 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Figma remained independent.

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:24.380 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
And because Figma later became
a public company, the post-deal

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:26.920 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
record became unusually transparent.

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:30.180 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Its own securities filings
preserved the abandoned Adobe

00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:34.280 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
transaction and the one-billion-dollar
termination payment as

00:13:34.280 --> 00:13:36.660 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
part of the company's financial history.

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:38.460 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
In July twenty twenty-five,

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:40.780 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
the company filed to go public.

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:43.160 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
And on August first, twenty twenty-five,

00:13:43.600 --> 00:13:45.800 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Figma completed its
initial public offering.

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:50.280 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The company sold twelve-point-five
million of its own shares at

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:52.420 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
thirty-three dollars per share.

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:54.300 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Its later filing reported approximately

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:57.800 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
three-hundred-ninety-three-point-one
million dollars of net

00:13:57.800 --> 00:14:00.460 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
proceeds before offering costs.

00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:03.920 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
That later success should not be
turned into a causal claim the

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:05.600 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
record does not support.

00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:08.220 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The public record does
not establish that Adobe's

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:12.780 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
one-billion-dollar termination
payment caused Figma's IPO, its

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:15.920 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
offering price, or its
later market value.

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:18.700 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
What the record does
establish is simpler.

00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:21.240 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Adobe did not acquire Figma.

00:14:21.240 --> 00:14:23.300 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Figma remained independent.

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:26.560 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
And less than two years after
receiving the termination fee, it

00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:28.260 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
became a public company.

00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:32.180 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
At the beginning, Adobe and
Figma negotiated the upside.

00:14:32.460 --> 00:14:35.060 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
A roughly twenty-billion-dollar
acquisition.

00:14:35.340 --> 00:14:37.680 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
But they also negotiated the downside.

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:41.440 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
What would happen if the required
regulatory clearance could not

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:43.800 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
be obtained under the terms of the deal?

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:48.180 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
That risk became a one-billion-dollar
reverse termination fee.

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:51.300 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Then the regulatory pressure became real.

00:14:51.340 --> 00:14:55.160 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The UK CMA published provisional
competition concerns and

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:56.500 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
possible remedies.

00:14:56.860 --> 00:14:59.680 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The European Commission
sent preliminary objections.

00:15:00.140 --> 00:15:02.140 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The Justice Department investigated.

00:15:02.340 --> 00:15:04.940 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Adobe and Figma disputed
the regulators' analysis.

00:15:04.940 --> 00:15:09.280 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
But by December twenty twenty-three,
the companies said they no

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:12.740 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
longer saw a clear path to
the approvals they needed.

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:16.220 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
So they terminated the
acquisition by mutual agreement.

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:19.660 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
And then the contract did exactly
what it had been written to

00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:20.460 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
do.

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:23.380 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Adobe paid Figma one billion dollars.

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:25.380 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Not because a judge awarded it.

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:27.660 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
Not because a regulator fined Adobe.

00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:29.500 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
And not because Adobe bought Figma.

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:32.680 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
The clearest billion-dollar
consequence of the failed

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:36.280 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
acquisition was a clause the two
companies had negotiated before

00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:38.780 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
the regulatory fight really began.

00:15:39.140 --> 00:15:40.617 line:78% position:50% align:center size:88%
That is what it cost.
